      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y+3z &=4 \\\\ x-\\frac{1}{2}y-\\frac{3}{2}z &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{3}{2} & -5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{3}{2} & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=-3,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, select: The system is inconsistent.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "957d2f35-7317-5ebf-a0be-8f624731712e",
