      ":question/id": "237a5249-3b4a-5172-b14f-5a8818ccf2a4",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+5y &=-11 \\\\ -x+2y &=-4 \\\\ x-3y &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 5 & -11 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 7\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 5 & -11 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1}\u2194{R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -11 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, select: The system is consistent independent.",
