      ":question/id": "29848cd4-a12a-5b93-8744-5b7c7ddb4226",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+3y &=1 \\\\ -4x+6y &=2 \\\\ 8x-12y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is inconsistent\nII. The system is consistent dependent\nIII. The system is consistent independent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 8 & -12 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 8 & -12 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -12 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(4){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is one free variable, $y$. Therefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true.",
